    "text": {
     "en": "A government works through three organs. The legislature makes laws, the executive carries them out and the judiciary decides disputes and checks if laws are followed.\nIn India, Parliament is the legislature, the Prime Minister and ministers form the executive and the Supreme Court heads the judiciary.\nSeparating powers prevents misuse."
    }
